<w:comments xmlns:wpc="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingCanvas" xmlns:cx="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/chartex" xmlns:cx1="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2015/9/8/chartex" xmlns:cx2="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2015/10/21/chartex" xmlns:cx3="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/9/chartex" xmlns:cx4="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/10/chartex" xmlns:cx5="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/11/chartex" xmlns:cx6="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/12/chartex" xmlns:cx7="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/13/chartex" xmlns:cx8="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/14/chartex" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:aink="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/ink" xmlns:am3d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2017/model3d" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:oel="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2019/extlst" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:m="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:wp14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:w10="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w15="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2012/wordml" xmlns:w16cex="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2018/wordml/cex" xmlns:w16cid="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2016/wordml/cid" xmlns:w16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2018/wordml" xmlns:w16du="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2023/wordml/word16du" xmlns:w16sdtdh="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2020/wordml/sdtdatahash" xmlns:w16sdtfl="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2024/wordml/sdtformatlock" xmlns:w16se="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2015/wordml/symex" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 w15 w16se w16cid w16 w16cex w16sdtdh w16sdtfl w16du wp14"><w:comment w:id="460" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="466E2C4E" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:pPr><w:rPr><w:rtl/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Give the Admin the same permission the Direct Manager has to "create and edit Objectives, KPIs, Targets and KPI Weights before the Employee's final approval, and update returned Plans."</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="507" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="01A9D329" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Give the Admin the ability to send the Plan back to the Direct Manager as a Draft if an edit is requested. The Manager can't make changes unless TD approves and returns it to them.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="508" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-26T14:05:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="3D985C52" w14:textId="761F8E0F" w:rsidR="000A457D" w:rsidRDefault="000A457D" w:rsidP="000A457D"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="000A457D"><w:t>the current BRD already supports the Return workflow. When a Plan is returned, the Direct Manager can make the required changes and resubmit it to the Admin for approval. Once approved, the Plan goes back to the Employee for review.</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:hint="cs"/><w:rtl/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> </w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="509" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-26T14:06:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="78ADAA2B" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="000A457D" w:rsidRPr="000A457D" w:rsidRDefault="000A457D" w:rsidP="000A457D"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:hint="cs"/><w:rtl/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">+ </w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="000A457D"><w:t>The Admin has visibility over the Performance Plan and can review it</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="6CDB4354" w14:textId="39663C97" w:rsidR="000A457D" w:rsidRDefault="000A457D"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="545" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="0F7E3C00" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Can we add the option to include an Employee in more than one Performance Cycle?</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="546" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-26T12:27:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="56A43D76" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>Allowing an employee to participate in multiple active Performance Cycles requires clarification on how evaluations should be managed.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="75D6BA78" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>For example, an employee may move from Business Analyst to Project Manager during the same year, with different Objectives, KPIs, Competency Templates, and potentially different Managers.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="49BC8F4B" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>This raises several questions:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="61D21A45" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/><w:numPr><w:ilvl w:val="0"/><w:numId w:val="59"/></w:numPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>How should the different evaluations be combined into one Final Annual Rating?</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="5446A3BB" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/><w:numPr><w:ilvl w:val="0"/><w:numId w:val="59"/></w:numPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>How should overlapping Annual and Semi-Annual Cycles be handled to avoid double-counting?</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="35040E88" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/><w:numPr><w:ilvl w:val="0"/><w:numId w:val="59"/></w:numPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>How should different Competency Templates and Manager evaluations be consolidated?</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="77AE49D3" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/><w:numPr><w:ilvl w:val="0"/><w:numId w:val="59"/></w:numPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>How should the final result be reflected in the Bell Curve?</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="74531C5C" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRPr="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04" w:rsidP="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00143E04"><w:t>We can either maintain the current approach of allowing only one active Performance Cycle per employee, or you may share the proposed evaluation methodology and Business Rules for handling multiple active cycles so we can assess the impact and incorporate the appropriate approach into the BRD.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="7286C00C" w14:textId="3373E73D" w:rsidR="00143E04" w:rsidRDefault="00143E04"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="609" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="71BDE638" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>When data syncs automatically from Jisr, all employees will be added. Can we remove employees who aren't part of the evaluation, e.g. external project staff, managed services, trainees, etc.? Or give the Admin the option to select which departments and sections are reflected on the evaluation platform.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="610" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-26T12:12:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="291D0959" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00717BA9" w:rsidRPr="00717BA9" w:rsidRDefault="00717BA9" w:rsidP="00717BA9"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="00717BA9"><w:t>This functionality is already covered in UC-006 – Create Performance Cycle. During cycle creation, the Admin can select the relevant departments, job titles, and employees, as well as exclude any employees who should not be included in the performance evaluation.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="32D6AC26" w14:textId="59FC540D" w:rsidR="00717BA9" w:rsidRDefault="00717BA9"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="614" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="73801FEA" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Their historical records are kept, but once their employment ends they should appear in the system as "Terminated".</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="682" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="7F8E3A6D" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>To be changed to Semi-Annual and Final only.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="760" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="436A07A6" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Allow the Admin to edit.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1093" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="5C75D88D" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Semi-Annual and Annual.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1148" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="3F5380F9" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Notify the Employee as well.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1445" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="6CC516C2" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Ability to download the files.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1451" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="6F89667D" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Edits can be made through the Admin.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1476" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="576D3491" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Give the Admin permission to add notifications, e.g. private notes or reminders.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1477" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-29T09:33:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="586D99AC" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="002A2A60" w:rsidRPr="002A2A60" w:rsidRDefault="002A2A60" w:rsidP="002A2A60"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="002A2A60"><w:t>Creating new notifications requires technical implementation, as notification triggers and recipients are managed by the system.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="7FAD4820" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="002A2A60" w:rsidRPr="002A2A60" w:rsidRDefault="002A2A60" w:rsidP="002A2A60"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="002A2A60"><w:t>However, we have added a Notification Management feature that allows the Admin to edit the content of predefined notifications, including subjects and messages in both Arabic and English, without requiring technical support for content updates.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="6172FF91" w14:textId="35B5025D" w:rsidR="002A2A60" w:rsidRDefault="002A2A60"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1636" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="0D79F174" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Also display the evaluation details based on the five SMART letters.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1687" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="21903CA3" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>The Admin can rephrase the Objectives.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1780" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="0F81E7A9" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>It shouldn't go to the Admin for review before being sent to the Employee. It should be sent to the Employee automatically, but shown to the Admin for visibility.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1905" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="47172DF5" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Translation option.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="1917" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="0ED57898" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Give the Admin the option to make Evidence mandatory or optional when the rating is 4 or 5.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2176" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-27T16:09:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="446F63C3" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0023598A" w:rsidRPr="0023598A" w:rsidRDefault="0023598A" w:rsidP="0023598A"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="0023598A"><w:t>Kindly confirm the calculation methodology currently used in the existing system to convert Competency Ratings (1–5) into a percentage-based Annual Competency Result, so the same methodology can be accurately reflected in the BRD.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="5EDFC6A1" w14:textId="00531034" w:rsidR="0023598A" w:rsidRDefault="0023598A"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2216" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="78EB5F67" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Competencies to be rated on levels from 1 to 5.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2415" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="5107229F" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Is this shown to the Employee?</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2416" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-27T16:27:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="6F4EAD26" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00AE33D4" w:rsidRPr="00AE33D4" w:rsidRDefault="00AE33D4" w:rsidP="00AE33D4"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="00AE33D4"><w:t>No, the Employee will only be able to view the published performance results, without the original Rating or Bell Curve calibration details.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="23E01441" w14:textId="38557368" w:rsidR="00AE33D4" w:rsidRDefault="00AE33D4"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2654" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="3F2DB589" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Show a notification.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2764" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="4A2ED027" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Talent Management Team</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2761" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="7CC634E0" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Give the Admin permission to edit the notification text.</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2766" w:author="Rahaf Hassan Asiri" w:date="2026-10-21T16:14:00Z" w:initials="RA"><w:p w14:paraId="5AE1E13F" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="0039062F" w:rsidRDefault="00CD76FE"><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:color w:val="000000"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>What does "Deadline Update" mean here?</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:id="2767" w:author="Sadeem Naif  Ganam Alharbi" w:date="2026-10-27T16:53:00Z" w:initials="SG"><w:p w14:paraId="4D74FCA0" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00133E0F" w:rsidRPr="00133E0F" w:rsidRDefault="00133E0F" w:rsidP="00133E0F"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference"/></w:rPr><w:annotationRef/></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="00133E0F"><w:t xml:space="preserve">“Deadline Update” refers to a change made by the Admin to the deadline of an ongoing or upcoming Performance Cycle stage, as defined in UC-008. </w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="27BED168" w14:textId="1C0C5421" w:rsidR="00133E0F" w:rsidRDefault="00133E0F"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText"/></w:pPr></w:p></w:comment></w:comments>